     * contained a sequence that never advanced the {@code position} index (e.g. a run
     * length of {@code 0}).  It also ignored the possibility of {@code -1} being
     * returned from {@link InputStream#read()}, which would cause the method to read
     * past the end of the stream and hang.
     * <p>
     * This version adds:
     * <ul>
     *   <li>Null‑argument checks.</li>
     *   <li>Explicit handling of {@code -1} (end‑of‑stream) with a clear exception.</li>
     *   <li>Validation that run lengths are positive and that the decompressed data
     *       never exceeds the size of the destination buffer.</li>
     *   <li>All reads are bounded; if the stream ends prematurely an {@link IOException}
     *       is thrown.</li>
     * </ul>
     * These safeguards prevent the method from looping indefinitely and protect the
     * application from a denial‑of‑service condition caused by malformed or malicious
     * input.
     *
     * @param in  the source stream, must not be {@code null}
     * @param out the destination buffer, must not be {@code null}
     * @throws IOException if the stream ends unexpectedly, contains an invalid run,
     *                     or the decompressed data would overflow the buffer
     */
    private static void decompress(final InputStream in, final byte[] out) throws IOException {
        if (in == null) {
            throw new NullPointerException("InputStream 'in' must not be null");
        }
        if (out == null) {
            throw new NullPointerException("Output buffer 'out' must not be null");
        }

        int position = 0;
        final int total = out.length;

        while (position < total) {
            int n = in.read();
            if (n == -1) {
                throw new IOException("Unexpected end of stream while reading run length");
            }

